module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.AffineTensorRecovery
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.PullbackSections.Affine
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Global sections of a tensor product over an arbitrary affine base

Let `S` be a scheme satisfying `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine` — not necessarily a spectrum on the
nose — and let `F` and `G` be quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-modules. This file proves that the global
sections of `F ⊗ G` are generated by the pure tensors of global sections of `F` and `G`, and
deduces that a morphism out of a pullback of `F ⊗ G` is determined by its values on those pure
tensors. Both statements are available on `Spec R` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.AffineTensorRecovery`; what is proved here
is the same content for an arbitrary affine `S`, which is the form in which a twisting of a
quadruple of Section 01NS is stated.

The passage from `Spec Γ(S, ⊤)` to `S` is along `j := (isAffineOpen_top S).fromSpec`, which is
an isomorphism, and it rests on one identification: **on an affine scheme the unit of
`j^* ⊣ j_*` is bijective on global sections.** That is `unitTop_bijective` below, and it comes
from `AlgebraicGeometry.restrictFunctorIsoPullback_hom_app_pullbackSection` together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection_top`: the unit on global sections is the
comparison of the restriction with the pullback precomposed with the inverse of
`AlgebraicGeometry.affineSectionsLinearEquiv`, and both of those are bijective.

With that in hand the comparison `j^*(F ⊗ G) ≅ j^*F ⊗ j^*G` of Tag 01CD carries the pure tensors
of global sections of `F` and `G` to the pure tensors of global sections of `j^*F` and `j^*G`
(`comparisonTop_unitTop_gammaTmul`), and the statement on `Spec Γ(S, ⊤)` transports. **No
scalars have to be transported**: a tensor product is generated by its pure tensors already as
an additive group, so the induction below uses only additivity and bijectivity of the composite
comparison, never the ring isomorphism `Γ(S, ⊤) ≅ Γ(Spec Γ(S, ⊤), ⊤)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral.gammaTmul`: the global section of `F ⊗ G`
  attached to a pair of global sections of `F` and `G`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral.unitTop`: a global section of `M`, carried to a
  global section of `j^*M` by the unit of `j^* ⊣ j_*`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral.comparisonTop`: the comparison of Tag 01CD read
  on global sections.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral.unitTop_bijective`: **the unit of `j^* ⊣ j_*` is
  bijective on global sections**, for every `𝒪_S`-module `M` and no hypothesis on it.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral.span_gammaTmul_eq_top`: **the pure tensors of
  global sections span `Γ(S, F ⊗ G)`** over `Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`, for `F` and `G` quasi-coherent on an
  arbitrary affine `S`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral.pullback_hom_ext`: **two morphisms out of
  `g^*(F ⊗ G)` that agree on the pure tensors of global sections are equal**, for
  `g : T ⟶ S` an arbitrary morphism of schemes into an affine `S` and `N` an arbitrary
  `𝒪_T`-module. Nothing is asked of `N`, so no quasi-compactness or quasi-separatedness of `g`
  enters.

## Implementation notes

`SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace)` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules S` are the same type by `rfl`, and the monoidal product in play
is `Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra.monoidalCategory`, whose tensor product on objects is the
tensor product sheaf on the nose. The two spellings are crossed by the abbreviations `ofScheme`
and `tensorMod`, as in `AffineTensorRecovery`, so that no comparison isomorphism appears in any
statement below.

Likewise `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction` for a morphism of
schemes and `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction` for the underlying
morphism of ringed spaces are definitionally equal, which is what lets `unitTop` — defined with
the ringed-space unit, the spelling the comparison of Tag 01CD is stated in — be computed by the
scheme-level lemmas about `Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute: Tag 01CE is carried by `AlgebraicGeometry.tensorSheaf_isQuasicoherent`
and Tag 01I8 by `AlgebraicGeometry.TildeTensor.gammaTensorEquiv`, and the statements below are
those results transported to an arbitrary affine base, not new results.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite AlgebraicGeometry MonoidalCategory
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineTensorGeneral

open Stacks.RingedSpace (structureRingSheaf pullbackFunctor pullbackUnit)
open Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence (tmul pullbackTensorComparison inv_val_app_apply
  val_app_inv_val_app pullbackTensorComparison_pullbackUnit)

attribute [local instance] Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra.monoidalCategory

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓ
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheaf Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsSMulCommClassΓ
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓPresheaf
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheafPresheaf
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheafVal

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine S]

/-- The structure morphism `Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ S` of an affine scheme, i.e.
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.fromSpec` at the affine open `⊤`. It is an isomorphism, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_top`. -/
abbrev fromSpecTop (S : Scheme.{u}) [IsAffine S] : Spec Γ(S, ⊤) ⟶ S :=
  (isAffineOpen_top S).fromSpec

/-- A sheaf of modules on a scheme `S`, retyped over the
`Stacks.RingedSpace.structureRingSheaf` spelling of the structure sheaf of rings, which is the
spelling the monoidal product of Tag 01CA is indexed by. The crossing of the `rfl`-equality of
the two spellings is done here, once. -/
abbrev ofScheme (F : S.Modules) : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace) := F

/-- The monoidal product of two sheaves of modules on `S`. -/
abbrev tensorSheafMod (F G : S.Modules) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace) := ofScheme F ⊗ ofScheme G

/-- The monoidal product of two sheaves of modules on `S`, retyped as an object of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules S`. -/
abbrev tensorMod (F G : S.Modules) : S.Modules := tensorSheafMod F G

/-- Tag 01CE for the monoidal product of two quasi-coherent modules on `S`, at the
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling of the category. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_tensorMod (F G : S.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [G.IsQuasicoherent] :
    (tensorMod F G).IsQuasicoherent :=
  @AffineTensorRecovery.isQuasicoherent_tensorObj S.toRingedSpace (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) ‹_› ‹_›

/-- The global section of `F ⊗ G` attached to a pair of global sections of `F` and `G`: the
image of their pure tensor under the unit of the sheafification that forms the tensor product. -/
@[sga "3 VIIA 3.1.2"]
def gammaTmul (F G : S.Modules) (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (t : Γ(G, ⊤)) : Γ(tensorMod F G, ⊤) :=
  tmul S.toRingedSpace (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) (op ⊤) s t

/-- The pullback of a sheaf of modules on `S` along `Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ S`, as a sheaf of modules
on `Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`. -/
abbrev pullbackMod (M : S.Modules) : (Spec Γ(S, ⊤)).Modules :=
  (pullbackFunctor (fromSpecTop S).toLRSHom.toShHom).obj (ofScheme M)

/-- The pullback of a quasi-coherent module along `Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ S` is quasi-coherent: that
morphism is an open immersion, so its pullback functor is isomorphic to the restriction functor,
under which quasi-coherence is preserved. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_pullbackMod (M : S.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent] :
    (pullbackMod M).IsQuasicoherent :=
  (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec Γ(S, ⊤)).ringCatSheaf).prop_of_iso
    ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback (fromSpecTop S)).app M) inferInstance

/-- **A global section of `M`, carried to a global section of `j^*M`** by the unit of
`j^* ⊣ j_*`, where `j : Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ S`. The preimage of `⊤` is `⊤`, so the target is the
global sections of the pullback with no transport along an equality of opens; the type is
ascribed at that spelling, which is what lets `rw` be used in a goal mentioning it. -/
def unitTop (M : S.Modules) (x : Γ(M, ⊤)) : Γ(pullbackMod M, ⊤) :=
  pullbackUnit (fromSpecTop S).toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme M) (op ⊤) x

/-- `unitTop` is additive. -/
theorem unitTop_add (M : S.Modules) (x y : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    unitTop M (x + y) = unitTop M x + unitTop M y :=
  Stacks.RingedSpace.pullbackUnit_add _ (ofScheme M) (op ⊤) x y

/-- `unitTop` carries the zero section to the zero section. -/
theorem unitTop_zero (M : S.Modules) : unitTop M (0 : Γ(M, ⊤)) = 0 := map_zero _

/-- On global sections the unit of `j^* ⊣ j_*` is the pullback of a section of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection` at `U = V = ⊤`. The two adjunctions — the
one of a morphism of schemes and the one of the underlying morphism of ringed spaces — are
definitionally equal, which is what makes this hold. -/
theorem unitTop_eq_pullbackSection (M : S.Modules) (x : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    unitTop M x = Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection (fromSpecTop S) M ⊤ ⊤ le_top x :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection_top (fromSpecTop S) M le_top x).symm

/-- **`unitTop` is the comparison of the restriction with the pullback, precomposed with the
inverse of the affine comparison of sections.** This is the identification that transports
statements about global sections from `Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S)` to `S`. -/
theorem unitTop_eq (M : S.Modules) (x : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    unitTop M x =
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback (fromSpecTop S)).hom.app M).app ⊤
        ((affineSectionsLinearEquiv M (isAffineOpen_top S)).symm x) := by
  have h := restrictFunctorIsoPullback_hom_app_pullbackSection M
    (isAffineOpen_top S) le_top ((affineSectionsLinearEquiv M (isAffineOpen_top S)).symm x)
  rw [LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply] at h
  exact (unitTop_eq_pullbackSection M x).trans h.symm

/-- **On an affine scheme the unit of `j^* ⊣ j_*` is bijective on global sections**, for
`j : Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ S`. By `unitTop_eq` it is a composite of the inverse of the affine
comparison of sections, a linear equivalence, with an isomorphism read on global sections.
Nothing is asked of `M`. -/
theorem unitTop_bijective (M : S.Modules) : Function.Bijective (unitTop (S := S) M) := by
  rw [show unitTop (S := S) M = _ from funext (unitTop_eq M)]
  exact (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _).comp
    (affineSectionsLinearEquiv M (isAffineOpen_top S)).symm.bijective

/-- The pure tensor of two global sections on a spectrum is the same element whether it is
spelled through the tensor-product-sheaf unit of `AffineTensorRecovery` or through
`Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence.tmul`; the two are definitionally equal. -/
theorem gammaTmul_eq_tmul (R : CommRingCat.{u}) (F G : (Spec R).Modules)
    (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (t : Γ(G, ⊤)) :
    AffineTensorRecovery.gammaTmul F G s t = tmul (Spec R).toRingedSpace F G (op ⊤) s t :=
  rfl

/-- **The comparison `j^*(F ⊗ G) ⟶ j^*F ⊗ j^*G` of Tag 01CD, read on global sections**, for
`j : Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ⟶ S`. -/
def comparisonTop (F G : S.Modules) (y : Γ(pullbackMod (tensorMod F G), ⊤)) :
    Γ(AffineTensorRecovery.tensorMod (pullbackMod F) (pullbackMod G), ⊤) :=
  (pullbackTensorComparison (fromSpecTop S).toLRSHom.toShHom
    (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G)).val.app (op ⊤) y

/-- `comparisonTop` is additive. -/
theorem comparisonTop_add (F G : S.Modules) (y z : Γ(pullbackMod (tensorMod F G), ⊤)) :
    comparisonTop F G (y + z) = comparisonTop F G y + comparisonTop F G z :=
  map_add _ _ _

/-- `comparisonTop` carries the zero section to the zero section. -/
theorem comparisonTop_zero (F G : S.Modules) : comparisonTop (S := S) F G 0 = 0 := map_zero _

/-- `comparisonTop` is bijective: the comparison of Tag 01CD is an isomorphism, and an
isomorphism of sheaves of modules is bijective on sections over every open. -/
theorem comparisonTop_bijective (F G : S.Modules) :
    Function.Bijective (comparisonTop (S := S) F G) :=
  Function.bijective_iff_has_inverse.2
    ⟨fun z => (inv (pullbackTensorComparison (fromSpecTop S).toLRSHom.toShHom
        (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G))).val.app (op ⊤) z,
      fun a => inv_val_app_apply _ (op ⊤) a, fun z => val_app_inv_val_app _ (op ⊤) z⟩

/-- **The comparison of Tag 01CD carries a pure tensor of global sections to the pure tensor of
the two images**, read on global sections over an affine base. -/
theorem comparisonTop_unitTop_gammaTmul (F G : S.Modules) (a : Γ(F, ⊤)) (b : Γ(G, ⊤)) :
    comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) (gammaTmul F G a b)) =
      AffineTensorRecovery.gammaTmul (pullbackMod F) (pullbackMod G) (unitTop F a)
        (unitTop G b) :=
  pullbackTensorComparison_pullbackUnit (fromSpecTop S).toLRSHom.toShHom
    (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) (op ⊤) a b

/-- The composite of `unitTop` with `comparisonTop` is additive. -/
theorem comparisonTop_unitTop_add (F G : S.Modules) (x y : Γ(tensorMod F G, ⊤)) :
    comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) (x + y)) =
      comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) x) +
        comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) y) := by
  rw [unitTop_add, comparisonTop_add]

/-- Every element `γ z` of the isomorphism of Tag 01I8 is the image under the composite comparison
of an element of the span of the pure tensors of global sections.

The induction is on `z`, and it uses only that the composite comparison is additive and
surjective on pure tensors: a tensor product is generated by its pure tensors already as an
additive group, so no scalar has to be transported from `Γ(Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S), 𝒪)` back to
`Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`. -/
private theorem exists_mem_span_gammaTmul_comparison_eq (F G : S.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] [G.IsQuasicoherent]
    (z : Γ(pullbackMod F, ⊤) ⊗[Γ(S, ⊤)] Γ(pullbackMod G, ⊤)) :
    ∃ x ∈ Submodule.span Γ(S, ⊤)
        (Set.range fun p : Γ(F, ⊤) × Γ(G, ⊤) => gammaTmul F G p.1 p.2),
      comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) x) =
        AffineTensorRecovery.gammaTensorEquiv (pullbackMod F) (pullbackMod G) z := by
  induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul s t =>
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (unitTop_bijective F).surjective s
      obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := (unitTop_bijective G).surjective t
      exact ⟨gammaTmul F G a b, Submodule.subset_span ⟨(a, b), rfl⟩, by
        rw [comparisonTop_unitTop_gammaTmul, ha, hb, AffineTensorRecovery.gammaTensorEquiv_tmul]⟩
  | add z₁ z₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      obtain ⟨x₁, hx₁, e₁⟩ := ih₁
      obtain ⟨x₂, hx₂, e₂⟩ := ih₂
      exact ⟨x₁ + x₂, Submodule.add_mem _ hx₁ hx₂, by
        rw [comparisonTop_unitTop_add, e₁, e₂, map_add]⟩

/-- **The pure tensors of global sections span the global sections of `F ⊗ G`** over an arbitrary
affine scheme `S`, for `F` and `G` quasi-coherent. This is Tag 01I8 on a spectrum, transported
along the isomorphism `Spec Γ(S, 𝒪_S) ≅ S` by `unitTop_bijective` and the comparison of
Tag 01CD. -/
theorem span_gammaTmul_eq_top (F G : S.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [G.IsQuasicoherent] :
    Submodule.span Γ(S, ⊤)
        (Set.range fun p : Γ(F, ⊤) × Γ(G, ⊤) => gammaTmul F G p.1 p.2) = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top fun x _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ :=
    (AffineTensorRecovery.gammaTensorEquiv (pullbackMod F) (pullbackMod G)).surjective
      (comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) x))
  obtain ⟨x', hx', e⟩ := exists_mem_span_gammaTmul_comparison_eq F G z
  have hbij : Function.Bijective
      (fun x : Γ(tensorMod F G, ⊤) => comparisonTop F G (unitTop (tensorMod F G) x)) :=
    (comparisonTop_bijective F G).comp (unitTop_bijective (tensorMod F G))
  exact hbij.injective (e.trans hz) ▸ hx'

/-- **Two morphisms out of the pullback of a tensor product of quasi-coherent modules on an
affine scheme that agree on the pure tensors of global sections are equal.**

Let `S` be affine, `g : T ⟶ S` an arbitrary morphism of schemes, `F` and `G` quasi-coherent
`𝒪_S`-modules and `N` an arbitrary `𝒪_T`-module. A morphism `g^*(F ⊗ G) ⟶ N` is determined by
the global sections it assigns to the pure tensors `s ⊗ t` of global sections of `F` and `G`:
the mapping property of a quasi-coherent module over an affine base reduces the equality to an
equality of linear maps on `Γ(S, F ⊗ G)`, which `span_gammaTmul_eq_top` exhibits as spanned by
those pure tensors.

Nothing is asked of `N`, so no quasi-compactness or quasi-separatedness of `g` enters. -/
theorem pullback_hom_ext {T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ S)
    (F G : S.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [G.IsQuasicoherent]
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace))
    {h h' : (pullbackFunctor g.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj (tensorMod F G) ⟶ N}
    (hyp : ∀ (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (t : Γ(G, ⊤)),
      AffineHomRecovery.sectionsMap g (tensorMod F G) N h (gammaTmul F G s t) =
        AffineHomRecovery.sectionsMap g (tensorMod F G) N h' (gammaTmul F G s t)) :
    h = h' := by
  refine AffineHomRecovery.hom_ext g (tensorMod F G) N ?_
  have heq : AffineHomRecovery.sectionsMap g (tensorMod F G) N h =
      AffineHomRecovery.sectionsMap g (tensorMod F G) N h' :=
    LinearMap.ext_on (span_gammaTmul_eq_top F G) (by rintro y ⟨p, rfl⟩; exact hyp p.1 p.2)
  exact fun x => DFunLike.congr_fun heq x

/-! ### The criterion in the shape a twisting's multiplicativity consumes

The multiplicativity condition of a twisting of a quadruple of Section 01NS is an equality of
morphisms out of `f^*𝒜_{id} ⊗ f^*𝒜_{jd}`, not out of `f^*(𝒜_{id} ⊗ 𝒜_{jd})`; the comparison of
Tag 01CD, which is invertible, mediates between the two. This section cancels it, so that such
an equality is reduced to a computation on the pure tensors of the pullback-unit images of
global sections — which is the form in which the section formulas of Tag 01CA compute both
sides. -/

section Tensored

open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction (opensMap)

variable {T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ S)

/-- The pullback of a sheaf of modules on `S` along an arbitrary morphism `g : T ⟶ S`, at the
`Stacks.RingedSpace.structureRingSheaf` spelling the monoidal product of Tag 01CA is indexed
by. -/
abbrev pullbackSheafMod (M : S.Modules) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace) :=
  (pullbackFunctor g.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj (ofScheme M)

/-- **The pure tensor of the pullback-unit images of two global sections**, as a section of
`g^*F ⊗ g^*G` over `g^{-1}⊤`. -/
def pullbackTmul (F G : S.Modules) (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (t : Γ(G, ⊤)) :
    (pullbackSheafMod g F ⊗ pullbackSheafMod g G).val.obj
      ((opensMap g.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj (op ⊤)) :=
  tmul T.toRingedSpace (pullbackSheafMod g F) (pullbackSheafMod g G)
    ((opensMap g.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj (op ⊤))
    (pullbackUnit g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme F) (op ⊤) s)
    (pullbackUnit g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme G) (op ⊤) t)

omit [IsAffine S] in
/-- **Reading a morphism out of `g^*F ⊗ g^*G` on global sections.** Precomposing with the
comparison of Tag 01CD and taking the effect on a pure tensor of global sections is evaluating
the morphism on the pure tensor of the two pullback-unit images. -/
theorem sectionsMap_comparison_comp (F G : S.Modules)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace))
    (u : pullbackSheafMod g F ⊗ pullbackSheafMod g G ⟶ N) (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (t : Γ(G, ⊤)) :
    AffineHomRecovery.sectionsMap g (tensorMod F G) N
        (pullbackTensorComparison g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) ≫ u)
        (gammaTmul F G s t) =
      u.val.app ((opensMap g.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj (op ⊤)) (pullbackTmul g F G s t) := by
  refine (SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.homEquiv_val_app g.toLRSHom.toShHom
    (pullbackTensorComparison g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) ≫ u) (op ⊤)
    (gammaTmul F G s t)).trans ?_
  refine (SheafOfModules.comp_val_app_apply _ _ _ _).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (u.val.app ((opensMap g.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj (op ⊤)))
    (pullbackTensorComparison_pullbackUnit g.toLRSHom.toShHom
      (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) (op ⊤) s t)

/-- **Two morphisms `g^*F ⊗ g^*G ⟶ N` that agree on the pure tensors of the pullback-unit
images of global sections are equal**, for `F` and `G` quasi-coherent on an affine `S`,
`g : T ⟶ S` arbitrary and `N` an arbitrary `𝒪_T`-module.

This is `pullback_hom_ext` with the comparison of Tag 01CD cancelled, and it is the form in
which the multiplicativity of a twisting of a quadruple of Section 01NS is checked: both sides
of that equation are morphisms out of `f^*𝒜_{id} ⊗ f^*𝒜_{jd}` with a known value on the local
pure tensors. Nothing is asked of `N`. -/
theorem tensor_hom_ext_of_sections (F G : S.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] [G.IsQuasicoherent]
    (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace))
    {u u' : pullbackSheafMod g F ⊗ pullbackSheafMod g G ⟶ N}
    (hyp : ∀ (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (t : Γ(G, ⊤)),
      u.val.app ((opensMap g.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj (op ⊤)) (pullbackTmul g F G s t) =
        u'.val.app ((opensMap g.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj (op ⊤)) (pullbackTmul g F G s t)) :
    u = u' := by
  have hc : pullbackTensorComparison g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) ≫ u =
      pullbackTensorComparison g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G) ≫ u' :=
    pullback_hom_ext g F G N fun s t => by
      rw [sectionsMap_comparison_comp, sectionsMap_comparison_comp]
      exact hyp s t
  have hiso : IsIso (pullbackTensorComparison g.toLRSHom.toShHom (ofScheme F) (ofScheme G)) :=
    Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence.isIso_pullbackTensorComparison _ _ _
  exact (@IsIso.epi_of_iso _ _ _ _ _ hiso).left_cancellation u u' hc

end Tensored

